---
description: Spec-driven Dostigus — read SPEC/ADRs, keep glossary stable
alwaysApply: true
---

Before writing code, read `docs/SPEC.md` and `docs/adr/`. Use only CONTEXT.md terms (Host not Host shell; MCP surface not MCP contract as the runtime name; Bot ≠ Module package; Builder not “cloud agent”). Do not invent synonyms. Docs and glossary are English only. Stay in SPEC scope (no agent runtime, Meal port, Builder Module-package writer, marketplace, Share link, guests). Household Members on one Host are in scope ([ADR 0012](docs/adr/0012-household-members.md)): the Owner adds Members; Members use Bot list and Chat. Settings, Bot create/delete, and Members stay with the Owner. Run `pnpm check` before commit.
